meta {
  name: Refresh
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
  body: none
  auth: none
}

vars:post-response {
  accessToken: res.body.data.accessToken
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.tokenType: eq Bearer
}

docs {
  Run Login first. There is no body and no Authorization header - the refresh cookie Bruno
  stored from Login is the credential, which is why this endpoint is public: by the time a
  client calls it, its access token has usually already expired.

  Every call rotates the token. The old one is revoked immediately, and replaying it is treated
  as theft: the server then revokes every session the account has, so the next Refresh fails too
  and the user has to log in again.

  The new access token is captured over the old one, so authenticated requests keep working.
}
